SwiftPutty local patch 0019
Upstream: PuTTY 0.85 (a3cce3a48d4ab12e0fccb32998b9042d4f7c3ff1)
Status:   not yet reported upstream; should be (a setting aborts)

Terminal: a negative scrollback size means no scrollback.

Every front end passes CONF_savelines to term_size() unchecked, and the
configuration box's "Lines of scrollback" accepts a negative number.
term_size() then failed its assertion that the scrollback fits the new
size, aborting the program when such a session started or the setting
was applied. Now a negative size is treated as 0. Applies after patch
0004. Found by fuzzing (Core/tests/fuzz/fuzz_parsers.c).

--- a/terminal/terminal.c
+++ b/terminal/terminal.c
@@ -2191,6 +2191,11 @@
     int sblen;
     int save_alt_which = term->alt_which;
 
+    /* A negative scrollback size (e.g. "ScrollbackLines=-1" in a saved
+     * session; the configuration box accepts it) means none. Otherwise
+     * the scrollback trimming below fails its assertion. */
+    if (newsavelines < 0) newsavelines = 0;
+
     if (newrows == term->rows && newcols == term->cols &&
         newsavelines == term->savelines)
         return;                        /* nothing to do */
